  2954	## D248 · 2026-10-30 · What counts as one question and one piece of evidence: seven boundaries, chosen one by one
  2955	
  2956	- Alex, on the census of duplicate and trivial questions: "我们的标准要收口"; then "你要不要深度的写好plan, 怎么测量，golden 是怎么，我们来解决这个问题；整体不能regress，你要秉持我们过往工程的原则，以及作为一个hedge fund analyst 到底怎么判断合并，去重，这个标准很重要，不能观点爆炸"; then, not following the plan's table, "我没理解每个难点，我需要一个一个和你过，你讲人话给我例子". Each boundary was put to him with an example and two options; his replies are quoted per row. Plan, census and review rounds: [question-identity plan](research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md) §0–§4, §11b, §12.
  2957	- The class ($0, `census/`): the sealed three-month run opened 69 questions in 59 days; Claude's reading of the first 50 (not reviewed by Alex) marks 12 duplicates and 10 that should not have opened, 5 borderline. Matching merged 39 of 122 candidates; the candidates opened new fall in three verdict classes (parsed from the decisions' reason text, not yet verified case by case): the collision judge's "distinct question in one matter", "same question" verdicts the code still opened (two traced to a model-written period start), and twins never compared.
  2958	- The principle, Alex after the seven answers: "我觉得核心就是这个颗粒度的把控要符合一个高端的hedge fund analyst 的思维。不要搜集一堆鸡毛蒜皮的事情，要看重要的大事，合并整合关键的信息，这个是这个步骤的原则" (written into AGENTS §8, "A senior analyst's granularity").
  2959	- Decided (the general rule under all seven: two questions are one when the same outcome settles both; they are kept apart only when their answers can move apart and an analyst would bet on each separately):
  2960	  1. **One plan, several wordings** (H1, "A"): wordings of one plan whose final check is the same number are one question; two numbers that move on their own and are watched separately stay apart; a single deal under a plan already opened by amount merges into it. Not put to Alex: a not-yet-signed deal's yes/no signing question (D210; PRD 06 keeps number and event questions apart) stays as it is and does not merge into a plan's amount question (the Ohio lease guarantee and the cloud-customer total in v38 both stay). Narrows the standard §4 "another quantity in the same deal (a guarantee beside a financing)" sentence taken from D190; consistent with D210.
  2961	  2. **One event, several deadlines** (H2, "A"): while the earlier-deadline question is open, a later deadline is its evidence, not a new question; when the earlier one falls due unresolved and the matter is still live, the system opens the next-deadline successor with the merged evidence, without waiting for a new article (new work for pull mode, D14, D54).
  2962	  3. **One product generation, several milestones** (H3, "A"): one question per generation, asked at the step that brings revenue (shipments begin); sampling and launch are its evidence; only milestones an analyst bets on separately (a drug's phase-3 data and its approval) are separate questions.
  2963	  4. **A company's own quantity by fiscal and by calendar year** (H4, "A"): only the fiscal year opens (PRD 06 ladder rule 5); a calendar-year estimate is evidence to the fiscal question, weighed lower when the years differ much.
  2964	  5. **A model-written period start** (H5, "A"): for event and policy questions it no longer blocks a merge; object, event and due day are still checked.
  2965	  6. **Small matters opened as questions** (H6, "A， A"): a deal, product or project (the question was put about small deals and products) opens a question only when its scale can change the company's revenue, profit, cash or credit risk; otherwise no question opens, and whether its statement is kept follows the evidence rule (standard §5). Done in this round together with the merge changes, each measured as its own arm, then together on the holdout. Narrows the standard §3 class C ("a sized, not yet completed stake or acquisition").
  2966	  7. **The same statement carried by several outlets** (H7, "A"): code treats pieces with the same known original speaker, original day and figures as one (an unknown speaker or day never matches: 297 of the sealed run's 4,298 pieces have both unknown); the judge sees it once with the outlet count; every piece is still stored. Changes D204's "both shown to the judge" for this case, and is a chosen exception to AGENTS §3 "equal values alone never establish identity"; the risk put to him with the question (a qualification such as "excluding China sales" hidden; D204's 8 of 40 wrong merges) is measured on the G3 gold before it is switched on, as is the accuracy of the original-speaker and original-day fields it relies on.
  2967	- Next, in this order: the signed standard page (§3 class C, §4 "same question, succession or another question") carries these rules, then a read-only Codex drift review; then the plan's step 1 (structured census, the fixed-extraction replay harness, gold G1–G3, the September holdout week on Alex's go).
  2968	
  2969	## D249 · 2026-10-30 · A test the model applies to each statement is a check at the end of the same request; role-v63 (`poc-v79`) measured, the default stays role-v53
  2970	
  2971	- Alex, after a second-turn probe judged statements by standard 5.1 correctly that the one-pass answer had kept: "那为什么你不在prompt 里面要求做完自己复核一边就好，这样就是一个call完成"; then "你尝试一组先吧，这个完全就是再prompt 的最后面要求做完一遍基于"你刚才说的复核条件"再跑一次；写在同一个提示词里面"; then "可以，但是这个做法是有效的对吧，那你应该好好地写复核的侧重点然后跑；这个如果有效可以记录下来这个做法"; then the goal "你需要让这个加到prompt里面的方式improve performance. 一定要improve but don't hardcode or break our principles".
  2972	- Decided (the method, written at AGENTS §6): from role-v59 the extraction request ends with a check that reads the evidence list back by standard 5.1 (`prompts/review-v<N>.txt`, `extraction.REVIEW_FROM`) and names no empty-answer condition; the role text of role-v59 to role-v63 is role-v53's. Every line of the check cites the standard (§5.1, §5.3, §6, D238, D243, D240); six read-only Codex rounds (`research/2026-10-30-noise/codex-review-*`); examples from other industries.
  2973	- Measured (run Y3, role-v53 and role-v63 sent together, development 118 + test 30 articles, three draws; `loop-log.md` rows 34–48): gold-rejected statements kept per draw 94.3 → 77.3 (−17, interval −33 to −2); core kept in every draw 72 → 74 of 86 and supporting in at least two draws 152 → 154 of 181 once a blind reader judged the 58 entries the counting aid scored differently (core draws 31 → 34, supporting 85 → 85); test supporting in at least two draws 38 → 41 of 42.
