1. **Use agreement or source-based adjudication to merge.** The code joins every group linked by either family. For Hugging Face, one reader linked closing to the U.S. and EU reviews, and the other linked closing to the outstanding obligation. That creates a five-entry group neither endorsed. Keep agreed merges provisionally and resolve disputed pairs blind against the articles. D248 requires the same outcome to settle both questions. [Group code](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/census_merge.py:313) · [D248](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2959)

2. **Merge the five-company capex duplicates within each year.** List items 2/24 and 3/25 cite the same $800B and $1.3T forecasts. The two source articles describe those figures as data-center capex and general capex, respectively, without establishing a separately measured data-center total. Keep the four-company totals, Alphabet alone, and the two years distinct. Also fold the **Ohio guarantee amount** into the total guarantees matter. The source puts the $105B Ohio guarantee inside the $108.5B total, and D248 puts a component deal under the existing amount question. [Capex sources](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/batches/batch-04.json:80) · [Ohio source](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/batches/batch-04.json:116) · [D248](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2959)

3. **Split Hugging Face.** Keep closing, the outstanding dollar obligation, and the separately accepted U.S. and EU reviews distinct. Use the generic regulatory entry as evidence for closing. U.S. clearance can arrive while EU review is pending, and neither settles the year-end dollar amount. Keep Anthropic’s deadline variants together around the single commitment decision. [Hugging Face source](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/batches/batch-11.json:233) · [Anthropic entries](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/matters-entries.json:329)

4. **Pin one scoring list before the first send.** The plan names the 38-entry `matters.json`. The dedup code writes a separate file and drops the example questions. Freeze one canonical question per matter, name the corrected file in the plan, and require its manifest hash when scoring. [Plan](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v10.md:116) · [Final-file writer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/census_merge.py:334)

